  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance to improve water resilience in the Sundarbans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government of West Bengal has requested the Government of the Netherlands for support on flood risk management.Key to the development of sustainable and safe Sundarbans is to ensure water security by developing resilience against floods, the creation of a freshwater environment on the islands and restoration of fresh water to the Sundarbans Delta. There has been a Dutch Risk Reduction (DRR) mission to give the West Bengal government the requested support. An overview of the possibilities of support has been given. The DRR report presents a visual roadmap for the development of the Sundarbans, which will form the basis for the consultancy services described in this Terms of Reference.In April 2022 a DRR mission visited the reclaimed areas of the Indian Sundarbans and the Sundarbans National Mangrove Reserve. The aim of the DRR-Team deployment was, together with the design engineers of the West Bengal Irrigation &amp; Waterways Department (IWD), the locally based Executive Engineers and Experts in Mangrove Development and Extension Services, to examine the situation, and to provide advice on what can be done both short- and long-term to improve flood resilience and water security. The mission identified two major focus points for improving the flood resilience of livelihood in the Sundarbans: (1) reconnection of the Sundarbans with upstream river systems, and (2) enhanced protection of the coastal area of the Sundarbans. This Terms of Reference focusses on the consulting services needed to support the Government of West Bengal with the second focus area: ensuring flood protection of the coastal area of the Sundarbans.</narrative>
  </description>
